WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.420
October 2022. Prices in
the UK are rising at 11.1

2
00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:09.460
per cent a year, the
fastest in over 40 years.

3
00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:14.750
By May 2024, that figure
has dropped to 2.0 per cent.

4
00:00:14.750 --> 00:00:17.810
A headline says inflation has fallen.

5
00:00:17.810 --> 00:00:19.820
Every number in it is true.

6
00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:22.550
But does that mean prices are now lower?

7
00:00:22.550 --> 00:00:25.600
So when every number in
a news story is true,

8
00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:28.270
how can the story still mislead you?

9
00:00:28.270 --> 00:00:30.410
In this mission, you'll
learn to read a data

10
00:00:30.410 --> 00:00:33.240
extract like an economist: units,

11
00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:36.680
levels, rates, and real versus nominal.

12
00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:39.080
Then you'll build an evaluation chain,

13
00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:42.100
from a first point all
the way to a judgement.

14
00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:45.460
Your mission: find out
how true numbers can still

15
00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:47.310
tell a misleading story.
